# Line endings are LF in the repository AND in the working tree, on every
# platform. This is not tidiness — its absence was a real defect.
#
# Without it, a Windows checkout converts source to CRLF. src/cli.zig's
# scaffold templates are Zig multiline literals, so the CRLF became part
# of the emitted app.ring; gates that regex on `\n` then stopped matching
# and reported success while checking nothing. Three suites failed in CI
# on a machine that had never touched the code (run 32581935566), and the
# same three passed locally, because the local tree had been written by
# tools rather than checked out.
#
# A build whose behaviour depends on how the source was checked out is not
# reproducible, and the difference is invisible in a diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary: never transformed, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.db binary
*.exe binary
*.wasm binary
